{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 5ff294e1: route A, host authority for every installed register\n\nRoute A. Any Worker that changes its register will meet this, so the fix belongs in the host adapters, not in a separate Worker. INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES already names the roots an operator keeps; host authority should follow the same list.\n\nScope of the source child, under parent 8a8902f3:\n- Both host adapters (Artifacts and GitHub) bind host authority to any root in the operator's validated installed list, not only ARTIFACTS_CONFIG.registerScope or its GitHub counterpart.\n- Keep every other check: the exact host and namespace, the pinned owner, the claim and directory birth at the destination's own register, credentials, and the GitHub repository binding.\n- New parentless creation still selects only the current REGISTER_SCOPE.\n- With no installed list, behavior is exactly today's single root.\n- Witnesses: after a switch, an old-root destination mints a read token and reads, on both adapter paths; an unlisted root stays refused; a pending old-root register operation still settles. The existing single-root cases stay unchanged.\n- Update docs/deploy.md: the installed list then covers host authority too, and its warning changes to match.\n\nLanding order:\n1. Land M1–M2 a41c09e4 now. It is approved (c0e4eef2) and ratified, it touches only packages/derive, and it does not conflict with this work.\n2. The route A source child, reviewed and landed.\n3. Revise the register packet f9941195 onto that main, keeping Register 17 installed and the old-room Git check after the switch and before the scratch room. Review it again.\n4. I deploy the packet and run the real commands, including the clone after its token's hour.\n5. Plan 035 M3 after step 3, or earlier while a review waits.\nO4 takes precedence whenever the browser connection returns. The mini stays off limits.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}